Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Do not seek during init when seekmode is linear no-rewind

With SeekMode < 0 the source must never seek, but initialisation still ran the
INITIALIZE_SOURCE stage, which does. Go straight to INITIALIZE instead.

--- a/src/core/videosource.cpp
+++ b/src/core/videosource.cpp
@@ -455,6 +455,11 @@
             }
         }
 
+        // If we are in linear no-rewind mode, don't attempt to seek during init.
+        // Bypass the INITIALIZE_SOURCE stage.
+        if (SeekMode < 0)
+            Stage = DecodeStage::INITIALIZE;
+
         // Cannot "output" without doing all other initialization
         // This is the additional mess required for seekmode=-1 to work in a reasonable way
         OutputFrame(DecodeFrame);
